  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Present perfect** → experiencia **sin decir cuándo**, o resultado actual.",
      "*Have you ever been to Scotland? — Yes, I have.* (no importa cuándo)",
      "",
      "**Pasado simple** → acción **terminada con un momento concreto** (dicho o implícito).",
      "*I went there in 2022.* · *What did you do there?* · *It was fantastic.*",
      "",
      "**Pistas de tiempo**",
      "",
      "| Present perfect | Pasado simple |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| ever · never · just · already · yet · so far · this week / this year (aún en curso) | yesterday · last night / week / year · in 2020 · two days ago · when · what time … |",
      "",
      "**Patrón muy frecuente:** abrir con present perfect (¿has…?) y dar los detalles en pasado simple: *Have you been to Rome? — Yes, I have. I went in 2022. We stayed for a week.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** nunca *present perfect + tiempo terminado*: *I've seen him yesterday* ✗ → *I saw him yesterday* ✓. Y *When have you…?* ✗ → *When did you …?* ✓."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I have seen him yesterday.",
        "right": "I saw him yesterday.",
        "note": "Con yesterday: pasado simple."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "When have you been there?",
        "right": "When did you go there?",
        "note": "Con when: pasado simple."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
